## 2026-07-28 (session 4)
Attempted: task 1.2 — file utilities.
Done: 1.2. `noctalia-core::files` (crates/noctalia-core/src/files/{paths,
  directory_scanner,file_watcher}.rs), a 1:1 port of src/core/files/*:
  - `paths`: assets_root()/asset_path() — env override (NOCTALIA_ASSETS_DIR),
    isAssetRoot's four-marker-file check, /proc/self/exe-derived candidates,
    installed/source fallbacks, OnceLock-cached like the C++ function-local
    static. INSTALL_PREFIX/INSTALL_DATADIR ("/usr"/"share") are documented
    placeholders — meson injects the real values at compile time; the Rust build
    has no install-layout story until the Phase 16.5 cutover. NOCTALIA_SOURCE_ASSETS_DIR
    is real (injected by a new build.rs from CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR, mirroring meson's
    `-DNOCTALIA_SOURCE_ASSETS_DIR`).
  - `directory_scanner`: scan()/is_image_path()/image_extension_filter(), incl. the
    exact tie-break chain (dirs always first; Size guarded to files-only, Modified
    NOT guarded so two dirs compare by mtime; case-insensitive name; raw name;
    abs_path as final tiebreak) and using fs::metadata (follows symlinks) rather
    than DirEntry::file_type (does not) to match std::filesystem::is_directory's
    symlink-following semantics; make_absolute mirrors std::filesystem::absolute
    (cwd-join, no symlink resolution) rather than canonicalize.
  - `file_watcher`: FileWatcher's raw inotify logic only (watch/unwatch/dispatch/
    fd) — not FileWatchPollSource, which is pure PollSource glue with no
    independent logic (verified in review) and belongs with calloop wiring
    (task 1.5) instead. Directory watch-descriptor ref-counting/sharing, the
    100ms per-watch debounce, and the raw inotify_event buffer parse (NUL-bounded
    name within the len-sized, kernel-padded field) all ported behavior-for-
    behavior.
  Added crates/noctalia-core/build.rs (first build script in the workspace).
  No new deps (libc already present from 1.1).
  Tests: 18 new unit tests (paths: asset-root validation + a same-process
    override integration test in tests/paths_test.rs, same OnceLock-caching
    reasoning as log's globals; directory_scanner: hidden-file filtering,
    extension filtering, sort semantics incl. the Size/Modified directory
