    unwatch/shared-directory-watch, since there's no reference C++ test to port
    from — none exists in tests/ for src/core/files/*).
  Pre-done review (rule 3) caught one real bug: dispatch()'s read buffer was a
  plain `[u8; 4096]` (alignment 1) cast to `*const inotify_event` (needs align
  4) — the C++ pins this down with `alignas(inotify_event) char buf[4096]`, lost
  in the initial port. Fixed with a `#[repr(C, align(4))]` wrapper struct; also
  added the review's suggested test for the Size/Modified directory-sort
  asymmetry.
